  "id": "unit9marrowstreet",
  "note": "UNIT 9, MARROW STREET — the empty one. A slim precast infill from the 2060s with a glazed\nstair bow on the front, three storeys, a shutter that has been down long enough to be tagged twice\nand a TO LET board nobody has taken down.\n\n⚠ IT IS THE ONE BUILDING HERE WITH NO WARM LIGHT, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN. Every frontage on this\nstreet glows after dark; a terrace where they all do reads as a strip of neon rather than as a\nstreet with businesses in it. This one has a single cold security lamp over the shutter and\nnothing else — its windows take a near-black `glow`, so they stay dark at night instead of being\nlit rooms in an empty building.\n\n⚠ ITS BOW IS FROSTED, NOT CLEAR. `ty_clone_vat` is the one `frost` palette in the table, which is\nexactly right for a stair core nobody has fitted out: a surface that is obviously glass and\nobviously has nothing behind it.",
